# A failed `+` must not leave shape variables bound. `S + T` fails on the
# dimensions (dimensionless vs length) after the shapes already unified, so
# `N` must stay free; `S + V` then solves N = 4 instead of hitting a stale N = 3.
# env: S: Matrix[N,N]
# env: T: Matrix[3,3] unit m
# env: V: Matrix[4,4]
X = S + T
Y = S + V
